From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:50:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: mediatek: btcvsd: stop the interrupt before unmapping

The handler reads and writes the PKV window, which remove unmapped while devres
still held the interrupt. An interrupt in that gap faults. Close the gate and free
the interrupt first.
---
 sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-btcvsd.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-btcvsd.c b/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-btcvsd.c
index 5e7e85b4c..8e1ecfff7 100644
--- a/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-btcvsd.c
+++ b/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-btcvsd.c
@@ -1384,6 +1384,8 @@ static void mtk_btcvsd_snd_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct mtk_btcvsd_snd *btcvsd = dev_get_drvdata(&pdev->dev);
 
+	mtk_btcvsd_snd_irq_disable(btcvsd);
+	devm_free_irq(&pdev->dev, btcvsd->irq_id, btcvsd);
 	iounmap(btcvsd->bt_pkv_base);
 	iounmap(btcvsd->bt_sram_bank2_base);
 }
